       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual limits for adults:** the maximum is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and a single dose is typically no more than 800 mg. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual single-dose limit.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. These risks apply even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day, a more typical analgesic dose)\n- **1600 mg/day divided differently**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
